description: Streamlit, FastAPI, and DuckDB patterns for Loupe
globs: "**/*.{py,sql}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Streamlit

- Pages in `src/loupe/ui/`; one concern per page (quality vs insights)
- Cache DuckDB reads with `st.cache_data` keyed on query params, not whole connections
- No secrets in code. Use env or `.streamlit/secrets.toml` (gitignored)

# FastAPI

- Routes in `src/loupe/api/`; Pydantic models for request/response
- API owns HTTP; domain logic lives in `quality` / `insights` / `data`
- Return JSON that Streamlit can plot; do not return raw DuckDB relations

# DuckDB

- One connection factory; read-heavy analytics in SQL, not Python loops
- Parameterized queries only. Durable files under `data/` (gitignored except fixtures)
- Prefer views for repeated quality/insight queries
